    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Johnson returns six weeks after starting sertraline 50 mg. He is a little better: he has written letters, though not his book, and walked out with a friend twice. He still wakes in the early morning with dread and reproaches himself for idleness. He has had five psychotherapy sessions and the first two sessions of behavioral therapy for tics, in which he is learning to notice the urge before the head-shaking tic and to answer it with a competing movement. He has no side effects. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>50 mg daily for six weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 15; GAD-7 9</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotherapy</td><td>Five sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Tic therapy</td><td>Two sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

